<</Length 1447>>
stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 50 760 Td (appropriate data processing agreements.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 50 742 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 50 724 Td (Rate limiting: LLM APIs have token and request limits. Build retry logic,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 50 706 Td (back-off strategies, and per-user quotas into your system.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 50 688 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 50 670 Td (Evaluation) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 50 652 Td (----------) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 50 634 Td (AI workflows are hard to test with conventional unit tests. Evaluation) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 50 616 Td (approaches include:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 50 598 Td (  - Golden set: curated input/output pairs reviewed by humans) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 50 580 Td (  - LLM-as-judge: a second model scores outputs against criteria) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 50 562 Td (  - User feedback: thumbs up/down, edit rate, task completion rate) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 50 544 Td (  - Regression suite: run on every model or prompt change) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 50 526 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 50 508 Td (Summary) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 50 490 Td (-------) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 50 472 Td (The right AI workflow pattern depends on task complexity, latency budget,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 50 454 Td (accuracy requirements, and safety constraints. Start with the simplest) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 50 436 Td (pattern that works, measure its failure modes, and upgrade complexity) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 50 418 Td (only when the simpler approach is proven insufficient.) Tj ET
endstream
